+# Module 2 — LLM Architecture Mechanics
+
+This CPU-runnable lab makes core LLM architecture concepts inspectable: causal attention, KV-cache accounting, low-rank adapters, a transparent signed 4-bit baseline, GRPO group advantages, and top-k MoE routing.
+
+It does **not** claim to reproduce FlashAttention-3 kernels, DeepSeek MLA, NF4/QLoRA training, AWQ, or production MoE systems. Those require model- and hardware-specific implementations. The optional GPU extension below is separate from the CI acceptance gate.
+
+```bash
+python -m venv .venv
+source .venv/bin/activate
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+pytest -q
+python -m app.evidence --output artifacts/evidence.json
+```
+
+## Optional GPU extension
+
+Run QLoRA on a small openly licensed model, record the exact model revision, dataset card, accelerator, package lock, seed, adapter artifact, held-out evaluation, peak VRAM, tokens/second, and latency. Do not compare results unless prompt set and decoding configuration are held constant.
